  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1151 AM CDT Fri Sep 25 2026\n\nMonday through Friday:\n\nUpper level ridging will return for Monday, while surface high\npressure lingers. Should be a pleasant day with partly cloudy\nskies and highs around 70. As the ridge heads eastward Tuesday,\nthe door will open for a return of deeper moisture into southern\nWisconsin. Precipitable water values are currently expected to\nincrease to around 1.5\" by later Tuesday into Tuesday night.\nA shortwave moving through late in the day or overnight will\nthen bring a return of shower chances to the forecast area. A\nfew rumbles of thunder will be possible as well, though \ninstability is looking rather weak at this time.\n\nModels are mixed with precip chances for the latter half of next\nweek, depending on how far south the deeper moisture gets pushed\nafter the Tue/Tue night system rolls through. There is the\npotential for quick moisture return late in the week along with\nmore shower chances. Confidence is on the lower end for precip\nchances late in the week given the model differences and that\nfact that this is still about a week out.\n\nTemperatures are expected to remain within a couple degrees of\nnormal through the extended forecast period.\n\nDDV",
